rong (though I think it's both wrong and scientifically shaky). I'm pointing out that even if you're right, the most effective rollout will be the one that behaves as if you're wrong. So for the sake of your project, you might set aside the biology question and just focus on what gets these particular engineers to adopt the workflow. That's where I think the levers still are.
